# Implementation Plan - Global Navigation Overhaul

# Goal Description
Address "poor navigation" feedback by implementing a unified, persistent navigation structure for the Consumer App.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> We will introduce a mobile-style Bottom Tab Bar for easier mobile navigation, in addition to a Sticky Header.

## Proposed Changes

### Layouts
#### [NEW] [apps/web/src/layouts/ConsumerLayout.tsx](file:///Users/shahbaz/Documents/Spendigo/apps/web/src/layouts/ConsumerLayout.tsx)
- **Top Bar**: Logo, Global Search, Cart Indicator.
- **Bottom Bar**: Home, Stores, Cart, Profile.
- **Content Area**: Scrollable area for page content.

### Routing
#### [MODIFY] [apps/web/src/App.tsx](file:///Users/shahbaz/Documents/Spendigo/apps/web/src/App.tsx)
- Wrap all consumer routes (`/`, `/store/*`, `/product/*`, `/cart`, `/profile`) inside `ConsumerLayout`.

### Page Refactoring
#### [MODIFY] [apps/web/src/pages/consumer/StoreList.tsx](file:///Users/shahbaz/Documents/Spendigo/apps/web/src/pages/consumer/StoreList.tsx)
- Remove ad-hoc header.

#### [MODIFY] [apps/web/src/pages/consumer/ProductDetail.tsx](file:///Users/shahbaz/Documents/Spendigo/apps/web/src/pages/consumer/ProductDetail.tsx)
- Should work within the layout (maybe hide bottom bar if needed, or keep it).

## Verification Plan
1.  Navigate between Home -> Store -> Product -> Cart.
2.  Verify the Navigation Bar remains visible.
3.  Verify active state highlights on the Bottom Bar.
